From 88ea82f884f1a3d05beae1564c2f4972455787cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:55:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 082/108] gpu: submit recorded commands before the command
 thread waits; WAIT_REG_MEM and fence-wait stats

VulkanCommandProcessor::PrepareForWait was a no-op, so when the command stream
waited (WAIT_REG_MEM on a guest counter, once per frame in Lightning Returns, or
the ring running dry) the commands recorded so far stayed on the CPU and the GPU
idled. Now they are submitted first (vulkan_submit_before_wait_min_draws, default 1).
Thor, Ark view near the big screen: 50.0 -> 42.2 ms per frame, GPU busy 66 -> 80%.
Also: gpu_log_wait_reg_mem (10-s stats), gpu_wait_reg_mem_sleep_us (finer polling),
fence waits on the command thread by caller.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

